<p>
<br />After some more crawling, Orkan stopped, making Wolfram almost bump into him again.  
<br />— <b>What this time?</b>— Wolfram frowned, adjusting his glasses.  
<br />— <b>We're here.</b>— Orkan was looking down through the ventilation cover directly above Edward's office.  
<br />— <b>Finally, get that cover off then.</b>— Wolfram tried to look past Orkan, but there wasn’t much room.  
<br />— <b>With what, may I ask?</b>— Orkan rolled his eyes.  
<br />— <b>With a screwdriver that is in your pocket, blockhead.</b>— Wolfram snorted. He knew Orkan just didn’t want to do anything and was acting stupid on purpose.  
<br />With a heavy sigh, Orkan finally pulled out a screwdriver and started removing the bolts from the ventilation cover. It didn’t take long before the cover came loose.  
<br />Orkan wasn’t exactly sure how he was supposed to get down, but with Wolfram stuck behind him, he had no choice but to go first. He tried to carefully crawl out of the vent, yet gravity quickly took over and he fell with a loud thud.  
<br />— <b>OW!</b>— Orkan hissed in pain after landing directly on his right elbow.  
<br />Wolfram only shook his head as he made his own way out. He was completely sure he could do it better somehow, but in the end he dropped down just like Orkan and landed badly on his shoulder.  
<br />Half a minute later, Wolfram managed to get up, rubbing his injured shoulder.  
<br />— <b>Get up, we just have to…</b>— He wrinkled his nose in pain. — <b>To find the statuette. It should be somewhere around.</b> 
<br />Wolfram started pacing around the office, scanning the place for the wanted trophy. Orkan followed soon after, looking for the treasure as well.  
<br />They searched everywhere, in the drawers, on the shelves and inside the cabinets, but it didn’t seem to be anywhere…  
<br />— <b>Found it!</b>— Orkan raised an arm with the Anubis statuette in it. Its perfect diamond edges caught the light and scattered it across the room.  
<br />— <b>Great!</b>— Wolfram rushed over, gazing at the treasure in awe. — <b>No wonder the client wants it so much, it's a masterpiece! A relic!</b> 
<br />— <b>Yeah… But I've had a ton of even better ones in my house.</b>— Orkan shrugged, fighting the urge to simply run off with the statuette rather than give it to anyone else.  
<br />— <b>Uh, okay.</b>— Wolfram wasn’t sure how he was supposed to respond to that.  
<br />A second later, the office door opened. Three people stood behind it, Edward and two security guards.  
<br />— <b>Oop, I guess we've found the rest of the team.</b>— Edward smiled playfully. — <b>Ah, I see, the Anubis statuette? It's good, isn’t it?</b> 
<br />— <b>It… It…</b>— Wolfram stuttered in shock. Why the hell hadn’t Brief warned them HE was there?!  
<br />— <b>Yep. So, you want to take it? Hehe. Right. Well it's just so unfortunate that I forgot to take the kettle off the stove! Whoopsie doopsie, I'd love to give it to you but I gotta go.</b>— Edward sighed and shook his head dramatically. — <b>I guess without me these guys would be able to use some force. Welp!</b> 
<br />Edward left the room with a cheerful whistle, leaving the elves alone with the cyborgs. Orkan squeaked and shoved the statuette into Wolfram's hands.  
<br />— <b>Don't hurt me, it was his idea!</b>— He gulped in fear, trying to put a little distance between himself and Wolfram as if that could prove his innocence.  
<br />— <b>WHAT?!</b>— Wolfram squeezed the treasure and threw it to the floor in panic. The diamond shattered into countless glittering pieces, covering the carpet with sharp fragments.  
<br />— <b>Don't care.</b>— One of the cyborgs raised a massive plasma gun. The weapon hummed as it began heating rapidly.  
<br />Orkan raised his hands in surrender, inching closer and closer to the window while Wolfram stood frozen in shock. The hum of the plasma gun grew louder, and Orkan decided to make one final move. He rushed towards the open window.  
<br />— <b>ORKAN, NO!</b>— Wolfram shouted, stepping towards his retreating teammate.  
<br />The plasma ray sliced through Orkan’s body like a hot knife through butter, splitting him cleanly in two. He didn’t even have a moment to process the pain. Both halves simply collapsed onto the floor, exposing muscle, organs and bone. The carpet was soaked with blood within seconds.  
<br />Wolfram couldn’t say a word. He had never seen a dead person before, especially not in such a gruesome state.  
<br />— <b>Wolfram, Orkan, get out of there right now! Edward is there, they just caught me!</b>— Brief’s worried voice sounded through Wolfram's earphone.  
<br />— <b>I KNOW! Just stand there below the office win</b>—  
<br />Another cyborg shot Wolfram in the hand. He had probably aimed for his head and missed. Wolfram screamed in agony as the bullet tore through his flesh, blood spilling down his clothes. With no other option left, he gathered all his strength, grabbed one half of Orkan’s body, hurled it through the window and jumped out right after it.  
<br />The third floor wasn’t extremely high, but the fall was still enough to break Wolfram’s uninjured arm. He barely stayed conscious. Adrenaline kept him awake, but it felt like hell.  
<br />— <b>Wolfram! Ork- Wh-what happened?!</b>— Brief stopped in front of one and a half elves, her eyes wide in horror. She felt just like Wolfram. She had never seen anything this horrifying before.  
<br />— <b>Unnghh…</b>— Wolfram groaned, his eyes filling with tears from both shock and pain.  
<br />— <b>D-d… Don't worry. Everything is alright.</b>— Brief took a shaky breath.  
<br />She looked up, but the security guards weren’t there anymore.  
<br />They probably thought that punishment was more than enough and had no reason to chase the intruders any farther. The orc pulled out her phone and started searching for something with trembling hands.  
<br />— <b>Let's go.</b>— She picked up Orkan’s half of the body, utter horror and pity written across her face.  
<br />— <b>Whh… Where to?</b>— Wolfram whined but forced himself onto his feet, his stance unstable and both arms bleeding.  
<br />— <b>To the mechanic.</b>— Brief looked away. — <b>He can't… Not like this… We must at least try.</b> 
<br />— <b>Mmh… I g… Guess so… Agh…</b>— Wolfram let out an agonised groan.  
<br />— <b>Do you need any…</b>— She reached one hand towards Wolfram.  
<br />— <b>N-no, no, I'm good!</b>— He couldn’t even force a smile, but he still refused any help… He didn’t want to show weakness, not in front of her.  
<br />— <b>Alright, then let's go.</b>— With that, Brief turned on her heels and hurried away, expecting Wolfram to follow.  
</p>
